  "knownLimitations": [
    "The relay sequencer is trusted not to present isolated clients with conflicting histories; no transparency or gossip layer is included.",
    "Key transparency and federation are not included.",
    "Konclave has not received an independent third-party security audit.",
    "Secure deletion depends on operating-system and storage behavior.",
    "Native attachment and general large-object transfer remain deferred; A2A exposes bounded artifacts and encrypted references.",
    "Arbitrary external A2A artifact URLs and automatic URL dereferencing are not supported.",
    "The native API requires explicitly injected identity, custody, authenticated journals and sealed MLS storage under one effective writer; its type signatures do not qualify a production backend.",
    "The bounded service example has fixed preprovisioned membership and an opaque relay fixture; it does not qualify live enrollment, HTTP relay authentication, WebSocket transport or a production database.",
    "Optional request admission cutoffs and receipts require negotiated signed support. The bounded service example rejects these options before admission rather than silently stripping them.",
    "Admission cutoffs do not cancel admitted work. Delivery observations are not proof of model execution, task success or exactly-once external effects, and never start model turns.",
    "The example's Windows atomic visibility and file sync are not power-loss durability; authenticated sealing and writer CAS do not detect coherent rollback, selective restore or deletion.",
    "The host owns and drains whole network-awaiting session futures before storage release; the shared session starts no background workers.",
    "Standard A2A translation terminates plaintext at the gateway; protected mode remains a separate fail-closed native handoff.",
    "This is an immutable source and SDK snapshot, not a binary, installer or marketplace publication, provider selection or deployment."
  ]
}
